As $\sum_k \stepsize_k = \infty$ and
$\gapfunc(x\opt, \epsilon_1, \epsilon_2) > 0$ for
$\epsilon_i > 0$, we have $D_\infty = 0$
with probability 1.

Now, fix $\epsilon > 0$, and let $\{x_i\opt\}_{i = 1}^N$ be
an $\epsilon$-net of $C \cap \mc{X}\opt$, where $N < \infty$.
As $x_k \in C$ for all $k$,
\begin{equation*}
  \min_{i \in [N]}
  \norm{x_k - x_i\opt} - \epsilon
  \le \dist(x_k, \mc{X}\opt \cap C)
  = \dist(x_k, \mc{X}\opt) \cas 0,
\end{equation*}
